  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) is clearly the dominant modality at 0.485 acc, while both image encoders are weak (~0.21-0.23). We have no data on whether multiprofile + aggregation can improve the RNA baseline. Question: Does switching from singleprofile to multiprofile with average-pool aggregation improve RNA classification, holding the encoder fixed at pca_n2000? Why this is best: config_002 is a minimal, controlled extension of config_001 (same encoder, same modality) that isolates the effect of the profile/aggregation design axis. Using avgpool (simpler) before transformer avoids confounding complexity. The result directly tells us whether multiprofile aggregation is a productive direction for the dominant modality, reducing uncertainty before committing budget to more complex multimodal or encoder-variant experiments."
}

